## Root Cause
Directly serializing user identifiers can expose sensitive information and make it easier for attackers to impersonate users.

## Explanation
The patch hashes the user ID before serialization, which prevents the exposure of sensitive user identifiers and makes it more difficult for an attacker to reverse-engineer user identities from the serialized data.

